ira — source provenance and licences
====================================

IRA project code and IRA-specific contributions are licensed AGPL-3.0-or-later
(see LICENSE). Imported portions retain their original copyright and licence
notices. docs/licensing.md describes the boundaries; no upstream ownership is claimed.

src/adb            Selected AOSP packages/modules/adb device implementation, Apache-2.0.
                   Original NOTICE and copyright headers retained. Host, TLS, compression
                   and non-Linux branches are removed directly. IRA's implementation is
                   in ira_*; local adaptations are marked separately as AGPL contributions.
                   cutils/sockets.h retains selected AOSP libcutils ABI declarations.

src/base           Selected AOSP system/core/libbase sources, Apache-2.0 (NOTICE).
                   Host logging uses stderr; Android31+ uses actual NDK liblog.
                   Unused tests, platform sources and headers are omitted.

src/auth           USB-only subset of AOSP frameworks/native/libs/adbd_auth and
                   system/core/libcrypto_utils, Apache-2.0. Original headers retained.
                   Provenance: README.ira.md and PUBLIC_KEY_SOURCE.md. System socket
                   discovery, wireless lifecycle and public-key encoding are omitted.

vendor/boringssl   BoringSSL crypto subset; fixed revision and changes in README.ira.md.
                   Apache-2.0 plus original third-party terms in LICENSE and retained
                   source notices. CMake source lists belong to IRA (AGPL-3.0-or-later).
                   Linux ARM64/x86_64 inputs only; SSL/PKI/tools/tests are omitted.

src/mksh           MirBSD Korn Shell R59c, MirOS/BSD-like licences in NOTICE and source.
                   IRA terminal changes and build integration are AGPL-3.0-or-later.
                   Magisk-derived su portions retain GPL-3.0-only; IRA additions are AGPL.

su integration    Magisk-derived portions in src/adb/ira_su_server.cpp and the mksh
                   su builtin retain GPL-3.0-only. They are combined with IRA's AGPL
                   contributions under the section 13 combination permissions of GPLv3
                   and AGPLv3. See LICENSES/GPL-3.0-only.txt; not an upstream relicensing.

src/zygisk        Hook implementations and framework Java are IRA code (AGPL-3.0-or-later).
                   api/zygisk.hpp is the unchanged Magisk API with its ISC-style licence.
                   zygisk_next_api.h is an unchanged ZygiskNext interface declaration;
                   upstream publishes no licence file. No new licence is assigned to it.

The Android NDK supplies libc, libdl, liblog, libc++ and public Android/JNI headers.
No duplicate copies are vendored. NDK r30 does not expose BoringSSL headers/libcrypto;
the crypto source subset remains necessary. Host tests use the selected NDK's public
log/JNI declarations and native host implementations for libc/threading.
